---
title: Sourdough starter
servings: 1
yield: 1 starter, about 150 g after each feeding
tags: [vegan, make-ahead]
time: 5 days 50 minutes
source: Sourdough Starter by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/sourdough-starter-recipe
---

== Day 1 ==

In a #glass jar{}(1/2 to 1 quart), stir the @whole wheat flour{50%g}(or pumpernickel flour) with @water{50%g}(cool) until no dry flour is left.

Cover loosely and leave somewhere about 70°F (21°C) ~{24%hours}.

== Day 2 ==

Weigh 50 g of the starter back into the clean jar and throw the rest away.

Stir in @water{50%g} and @all-purpose flour{50%g}. Cover loosely and leave ~{24%hours}.

== Days 3 to 5 ==

Feed it twice a day, about 12 hours apart. Each time, keep 50 g of starter, discard the rest, and stir in another 50 g water and 50 g all-purpose flour.

Use cool water when the kitchen is warm and lukewarm water when it is cool.

The starter is ready when it at least doubles within 6 to 8 hours of a feeding, is full of bubbles and smells pleasantly sour. If it is not there by day 5, keep feeding every 12 hours for a day or two more.

> It is happiest between 70°F and 78°F (21°C to 26°C). Below 68°F, find it a
> warmer spot, such as the top of the fridge or the oven with only the light on.

> For a bigger starter, begin with 113 g flour and 113 g water, keep 113 g at
> each feeding and feed it 57 g flour and 57 g water.
